00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:11,400
Example 2: Compare numbers 32 and 28.

2
00:00:13,970 --> 00:00:18,330
Fill in the blank.

3
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:31,240
Number 32 consists of 3 tens and 2 ones

4
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:43,700
Number 28 consists of 2 tens and 8 ones

5
00:00:45,370 --> 00:00:57,740
Numbers 32 and 28 have different tens digits, so we compare the tens digits of these two numbers.

6
00:00:58,970 --> 00:01:08,480
We see 3 > 2, so 32 > 28

7
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:19,890
Comparing two-digit numbers.

8
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:32,490
First, we compare the tens digits of the two numbers.

9
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:44,940
If the tens digit of one number is greater, then that number is greater.

10
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:59,540
If the tens digits of the two numbers are equal, we compare the ones digits of the two numbers.

11
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:13,060
At that point, the ones digit of whichever number is greater, that number is greater.

